               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 73-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without pneumonic infiltrates. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was promptly treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout his stay. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged in stable condition with instructions to continue inhaled bronchodilators and a tapering course of oral steroids. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
